src/quest/harness.ml:2611:  Engine is derived from the Run InitRecord, never stated. Finds the tape like find-tape, then blocks in code: streams NDJSON lifecycle_change rows and ends with one verdict {ok, run_id, harness, session_id, wal, pid, outcome, settled, lifecycle}.\n\
src/quest/harness.ml:2628:  For a link-claimed Run, writes tape_path into runs/<run_id>.json in one atomic write; the binding is pinned: re-binding the same tape is a no-op, a different tape is E_EXISTS. For a legacy Run with only an InitRecord, appends one pointer-only tape_binding row to <git-common-dir>/bp3/run-lifecycle-derivations/<run-id>.jsonl. A run-id with neither is E_NOT_FOUND; a bad run-id or a missing, duplicate, or =-formed flag is E_USAGE. Emits {ok, run_id, tape_path, path}.\n\
src/quest/harness.ml:2647:  Reads every .jsonl tape under the corpus (default: the engine's tape source), folds mechanical facts per tape (BP3_RUN_ID bindings, bp3 invocations, E_* refusals, commit shas, finish/exit evidence, torn tails; pi tapes also yield session-id, entry counts, and summed usage) and emits one verdict {ok, engine, corpus, tapes_replayed, identifiable, traces, findings}. Each finding names its tape, run-id, evidence lines, and proposed fix target (dispatcher, adapter, contract; muse findings keep bp3 q u / hooks). A parser crash fails the call; findings themselves never gate. Truncated, foreign, and torn tapes are reported in findings, never fatal. Replay is deterministic: same corpus, same verdict.\n\
